{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/854629-best-families-to-go-with-a-beast-setting","id":854629,"title":"Best families to go with a BEAST setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T13:18:05-07:00","id":854629,"title":"Best families to go with a BEAST setting","content":"I've been thinking which supernatural go best with a Beast crossover, I've been thinking demons &amp; Changelings but I'd like to know others thoughts. I'm new to world of darkness in general and I don't know too much about other races other than BEAST. Any advice would be appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T13:29:07-07:00","id":854636,"title":"","content":"Beasts tend to like Changelings, and regard them as kin. They also have the dream linkage, which gives them commonality (as long as the Beasts don't go on too much about how they also feel about the True Fae being kin.) Beasts and Demons, however, don't get on. It always seems to end in violence between them, and they are most definitely NOT kin- being artificial constructs.<br /> <br /> Of course, being at odds with each other is no reason to not have them as a fun source of conflict in a crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T13:34:55-07:00","id":854638,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the easiest one to crossover with Beast would probably be Vampire, as it doesn't have all the esoteric metaphysics of some of the other gamelines and is fairly understandable. When you first mention the fangs, people know it's a vampire. That said, vampires aren't so good as player characters in a crossover. They make for excellent connections, allies or antagonists however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:41:23-07:00","id":854678,"title":"","content":"My ideal crossover team consists of a Werewolf, a Changeling, a Sin-Eater, a Demon, and a Beast. The Uratha, Lost, Bound, and Begotten all have good synergy with each other and can really build each other up with pack mechanics, oaths( if/when we make a non-changeling version), the Krewe ceremony, and the Beast doing what the Beast does. The Demon adds a little to that, creates some sibling rivalry, and adds a little punch and a lot of other things.<br /> <br /> This team up also doesn't face some of the time problems that working with a Vampire, Mummy or Promethean(Granted, they have way more time than they used to) have, and it neatly sidesteps a lot of the issues having a Mage could potentially bring up. That said, Vampires, Mages, and Prometheans make a good fifth if you don't like Demon as much. Mummy's a little harder to recommend just because their default state enourages a sort of orbit around them and their way of un/life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:25:36-07:00","id":854779,"title":"","content":"Well I meant more the other factions in the setting not necessarily part of the family - though I do consider that. More of storywise what races bring out some interesting thoughts to Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:41:50-07:00","id":914461,"title":"","content":"Mages: I had some trouble figuring out why Mages are even considered kin by Beasts- certainly most of them don't consider themselves monsters or Monsters, and would probably give a Beast insisting otherwise some side-eye. So there's some good drama to be mined there. I don't view the Beast-kin thing as something that's literally true: I like the idea that all the monsters are connected instead by the scars they've left on humanity's collective unconscious; even kinship Nightmares aren't about aping a family's methods, but about taking inspiration from what makes them scary. Mages, therefore are closer to that definition of Monster then they'd like to believe: people <i>remember</i> Atlantis and the Ladder on some level, filtered through legends. The Quiescience marks nearly everyone, and the Abyss resonates strongly with the absolute worst of human experiences. If I was running it, I'd probably enforce the idea that Beasts can only feed by hurting people, even through a Family Dinner. They couldn't just watch some Mage solve a mystery or recharge their batteries by doing yoga by a Hallow or drinking Tass-whiskey or whatever - You'd need Oblations involving pain, blood sacrifice, soul stealing, i.e. properly monstrous acts. The idea is to confront the Mages with the damage their own hungers can do, even if they don't partake themselves.<br /> <br /> Changelings: Changelings, on the other hand, are perfectly aware they're heir to a monstrous legacy they didn't choose, but Changeling is all about what happens afterwards. Some of them are perfectly, whimsically monstrous, while others try to get away from that and re-define themselves. Both have good resonance with Beast - I'd be a little leery about this, though, just because Changeling's abuse themes and Beast's abuser themes could go badly wrong together. On the other hand, I also like the contrast between the primal unconsiousness that Beasts draw from and Wyrd - in particular, Wyrd can be loop-holed but not outright defied, while the primal unconscious can set you up for a role (monster, Hero) but can't actually make you follow through. A Beast raging against their fate could be inspirational to a Changeling, while a Hero with Changeling backup gives the Monomyth a shitload of new teeth. (Best NOT to have the Beast ID more with Gentry than the Changelings if you want a cooperative crossover). In this crossover, I might let Beasts Family Dinner off non-monstrous acts, just because Changeling's a bit more hopeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}